<title>USA: USDA, China to meet on poultry dispute next week.</title>
<headline>USDA, China to meet on poultry dispute next week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. and Chinese poultry experts were expected to meet next week in Beijing to discuss a potential ban on U.S. poultry exports, an Agriculture Department official said Friday.</p>
<p>Paul Drazek, senior trade adviser to Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman, told USDA's radio news service that two USDA experts were to meet their Chinese counterparts on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Hopefully, some of the misunderstanding that exists on the poultry issue can be cleared up fairly quickly,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>China has threatened to cut off poultry exports from 10 U.S. states for fear it might carry a serious strain of avian influenza. U.S. officials say the disease does not exist in the United States.</p>
